Description: pvr: keep deferred DBSC patch locations valid
 For a secondary command buffer with a deferred control stream,
 pvr_emit_ppp_state() reserves two dwords for a PPP state update in the
 host-side stream and stores a pointer to them in a
 PVR_DEFERRED_CS_COMMAND_TYPE_DBSC command. pvr_execute_deferred_cmd_buffer()
 writes VDMCTRL_PPP_STATE0/1 through that pointer in vkCmdExecuteCommands().
 The stream is a util_dynarray (deferred_cs_mem) that is reallocated when it
 grows, starting at 64 bytes, so the stored pointer refers to freed memory as
 soon as later commands of the secondary enlarge the stream. The PPP state
 words in the copied stream then keep their uninitialized contents, and the
 write goes to freed heap memory.
 .
 Store the control stream and the dword offset instead of the pointer and
 compute the address when the command is executed.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
